<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady on limited supply.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady on limited supply.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in the Indore market of central India on Thursday while other major markets were closed for a local festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on limited supplies from processing plants and refineries due to poor availability of soybean.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up by 600 rupees and soyoil refined was up by 300 rupees per tonne. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction was steady but the undertone was dull due to limited export demand.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $278-279 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $131-132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,525 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,500 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. The undertone was steady.</p>
